1
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:13,060
Punch is incoming! Two in a row!

2
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:42,200
His ice breath is next!

3
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:50,340
Coming up in three, two, one, now!

4
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,500
Now it's our turn! Wow!

5
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:34,137
I was always in the light of the night
I was not even in the sky I was not able

6
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:37,737
to reach my feet I was not able to reach

7
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:44,020
the sky I was not able to reach the sky

8
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:39,837
Do naiyume ka sa ne te Izu

9
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:44,120
aru Cait no nai ano hikari wo

10
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:47,700
Oh, give it for my way

11
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:08,777
Attack batter, it's changing!

12
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:11,340
Stay sharp! Oh my god. Kazuto!

13
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:13,617
There's only three clear spots left.

14
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:17,112
Can't you use that skill
connector thingy you used before?

15
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:20,660
He's still got two bars
left on his HP gauge.

16
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:23,531
Skill connect won't even put a dent in it.

17
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:27,470
Watch out!

18
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:28,875
Ice breath coming up!

19
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:41,260
Oh no, the buff!

20
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:43,238
Hazard, don't wait!

21
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:13,140
Get out of there!

22
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:28,270
Xenon!

23
00:04:28,353 --> 00:04:29,472
Keep him busy for a few!

24
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:45,417
Swordsman, if we continue this course
of action, we will not defeat Thrymmer.

25
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:47,080
There is but one hope now.

26
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:50,297
Somewhere in this room,
hidden in the plunder,

27
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:53,500
you will find the treasure
of my people. I'm on it.

28
00:04:53,660 --> 00:04:55,957
Tell me what it looks
like and I'll grab it.

29
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,740
It is about yea big.

30
00:04:58,140 --> 00:04:59,920
It is a hammer made of gold.

31
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:01,700
Wait, it's a hammer?

32
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:16,280
Hey, Kazuto, you can find it using a
lightning skill! Lightning? Really?

33
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:41,040
There it is.

34
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:52,300
Freya! Chance!

35
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:03,680
It flows into me.

36
00:06:06,140 --> 00:06:07,540
Freya?

37
00:06:09,980 --> 00:06:14,300
Through me, it overflows.

38
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:17,110
No!

39
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:21,670
Freya?

40
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:32,840
She's a...

41
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:35,500
A friggin' dude!

42
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:42,920
Oh, he's Thor, the god of thunder.

43
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:47,110
Hmm?

44
00:06:51,460 --> 00:06:53,240
You despicable giant!

45
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:56,520
Your treachery and deceit
has come to an end,

46
00:06:56,660 --> 00:06:59,680
and now you shall pay
for stealing Mjolnir!

47
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:11,700
I shall make you pay for deceiving
me, you miserable excuse of a god!

48
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:17,280
I shall rip that beard from your face
and send your buddy back to Asgard!

49
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:20,217
Thor's pulling aggro from Thrymmer.

50
00:07:20,300 --> 00:07:21,829
Let's attack while we can.

51
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:25,537
Here we go, guys! Hit him
hard! Don't hold back!

52
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:27,149
Use all your sword skills!

53
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:05,600
This is it!

54
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:29,820
Return to your abyss, King of the Diets!

55
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:43,680
AVAILABLE NOW Revel in
your victory, insects!

56
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:49,040
But take heed if you put your
faith in the dogs of Aesir!

57
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:05,700
You have my gratitude,
brave fairy warriors.

58
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:11,080
Thanks to you, my treasure has been
returned and my disgrace avenged.

59
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:13,980
Now then, I must reward you.

60
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:23,280
That is Mjolnir, the lightning hammer.

61
00:09:23,660 --> 00:09:25,420
Use it in noble battles.

62
00:09:26,340 --> 00:09:28,020
Farewell, my champions.

63
00:09:48,260 --> 00:09:49,140
Congrats, pal.

64
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:51,020
You got a legendary weapon.

65
00:09:51,220 --> 00:09:53,380
Yeah, but it's a hammer.

66
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:55,426
I don't got no hammer skills.

67
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:04,100
The room's moving!

68
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:07,020
Wait, is it floating?

69
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:10,160
Hey, Kazucho?

70
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:13,340
I don't think this quest is over yet. Huh?

71
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:17,820
Good fairies, infiltrate Thrymheim.

72
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:21,480
Remove Excalibur from its
plinth and save my realm.

73
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:22,957
Look at the medallion.

74
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:25,746
It's all black except
for that one clear spot.

75
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:27,330
Daddy!

76
00:10:27,413 --> 00:10:31,880
A stairway leading down has just
appeared behind the throne! Seriously?

77
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:42,920
Let's go!

78
00:10:59,340 --> 00:11:00,300
System command!

79
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:01,741
Generate object!

80
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:03,180
ID Excalibur!

81
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:09,340
Long time no see.

82
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,720
You got it, Kirito!

83
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:20,220
Come on, pull harder!

84
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:21,614
Put your back into it!

85
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:24,140
Don't give up, Daddy!

86
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:25,640
You can do it!

87
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:26,995
I know you can do it!

88
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:28,620
Don't keep pulling!

89
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:56,857
Oh, crap.

90
00:11:56,940 --> 00:11:58,920
It's breaking up!

91
00:12:04,820 --> 00:12:05,650
Daddy!

92
00:12:05,733 --> 00:12:06,832
Thrymheim is collapsing!

93
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:08,609
We have to leave here now!

94
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:09,780
I know, I know!

95
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:16,670
Alright!

96
00:12:16,900 --> 00:12:19,277
Looks like it's up to me to save the day!

97
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:21,960
Time for some Olympic grade high jumping!

98
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:28,250
Ow!

99
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:53,020
We're so screwed.

100
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:55,160
Leafa, how much time we got?

101
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:57,340
We made it!

102
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:58,940
Thank God!

103
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:00,820
We made it!

104
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:03,970
Yeah.

105
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:10,840
Looks like I can't claim Excalibur
unless the quest is cleared.

106
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:17,240
Did you hear that? Huh?

107
00:13:20,620 --> 00:13:21,760
There it is again.

108
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:29,390
Tonki!

109
00:13:32,180 --> 00:13:33,220
We're saved!

110
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:34,460
Hurry, guys.

111
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:35,680
Hop on his back.

112
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:42,677
We're running out of time.

113
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:43,720
Yeah, I know.

114
00:13:46,460 --> 00:13:49,400
Wish it wasn't so high up. Go on. Jump!

115
00:13:55,340 --> 00:13:56,480
Hey, Donkey.

116
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:58,400
Thanks for saving my ass.

117
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:06,740
I guess you're still too heavy for me.

118
00:14:07,540 --> 00:14:08,370
Daddy?

119
00:14:11,580 --> 00:14:13,960
Seriously, stupid cardinal system.

120
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:43,720
That's about 200 meters.

121
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:57,440
Eku, Ski-Ta, Aftal, Eil

122
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:05,020
You gotta be kidding?

123
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:14,790
Heavy!

124
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:18,220
C! C! C! C!

125
00:15:18,340 --> 00:15:19,280
C-9!

126
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:20,780
That was awesome!

127
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:25,868
Don't look at me like that.

128
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:27,021
You can have it.

129
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:29,160
Here. Thanks!

130
00:15:29,480 --> 00:15:30,540
You're the best!

131
00:15:31,420 --> 00:15:34,008
I'll give it to you,
but with one condition.

132
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:35,620
You gotta promise me.

133
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:41,080
Every time you dry, you have
to think about me, okay?

134
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:46,700
Well, well.

135
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,353
The chick magnet's got another girl's...

136
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:53,620
You got it.

137
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:56,177
I'll think about you every time I try it.

138
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:57,090
Thanks a lot.

139
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,711
You're more than welcome.

140
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:14,820
Man, this sucks.

141
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:18,177
We only got to do one quest in
it, and now it's gone for good.

142
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:19,090
I know.

143
00:16:19,173 --> 00:16:20,728
It seems like such a waste.

144
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:12,660
Look at that, it's sprouting!

145
00:17:24,840 --> 00:17:26,480
It's so warm.

146
00:17:26,900 --> 00:17:28,420
So warm.

147
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:47,360
He's happy.

148
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:19,480
I'm happy, too.

149
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:22,812
Isn't this great, Tonki?

150
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:27,380
Look, all your friends have
come to say hi. You see them?

151
00:18:27,580 --> 00:18:28,760
They're all waving.

152
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:30,715
You're a popular guy.

153
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:39,000
He removed Excalibur from its plinth.

154
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:41,220
The quest has been completed.

155
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:45,577
Now that the sword which
slices wood and iron is secure,

156
00:18:45,660 --> 00:18:48,320
Jotunheim can return to its former glory.

157
00:18:48,620 --> 00:18:51,320
It is all thanks to you and your bravery.

158
00:18:51,720 --> 00:18:56,600
My younger sisters would also like to
express their gratitude towards you.

159
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:02,380
My name is Berdandi.

160
00:19:02,820 --> 00:19:03,820
Thank you,

161
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:09,200
oh brave fairy warriors, to think I
can gaze upon a green Jotunheim again.

162
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:11,320
Oh, it's like a dream.

163
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:22,600
And my name is Sculpt.

164
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:25,080
You have my thanks and respect.

165
00:19:35,520 --> 00:19:39,000
My gift to you shall be the Holy Sword.

166
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:47,760
Yes!

167
00:19:48,860 --> 00:19:51,500
Thank you, noble fairies.

168
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:53,280
Until we meet again.

169
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:57,060
We finally cleared it.

170
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:11,180
Um, excuse me, Lady Skolt?

171
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:12,760
Can I get your number?

172
00:20:44,600 --> 00:20:47,480
Right now, I respect you
more than ever, Klein.

173
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:50,260
You can be a dork, but you got heart.

174
00:20:58,280 --> 00:20:59,221
How's that, Yui?

175
00:20:59,980 --> 00:21:01,620
I can see perfectly, Daddy!

176
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:03,040
And I can hear, too!

177
00:21:03,820 --> 00:21:05,417
Cool, but what is it?

178
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:09,460
I'm turning real-time footage
of the cafe into mock 3D images.

179
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:12,240
Okay, try moving, but take it slow.

180
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:13,830
Okay!

181
00:21:18,820 --> 00:21:23,157
If it's working right, Huey should
feel like she's flying around the room.

182
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:24,320
I get it.

183
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:27,977
That camera and its mic are
acting like Huey's eyes and ears.

184
00:21:28,060 --> 00:21:30,297
Gotta hand it to you,
that's pretty clever.

185
00:21:30,380 --> 00:21:32,457
Kazuto's taking a class called Mecho...

186
00:21:32,540 --> 00:21:33,620
Mecha-something.

187
00:21:33,720 --> 00:21:34,880
It's mechatronics.

188
00:21:35,500 --> 00:21:38,117
Like I was saying, he's
taking this Mecha-thing class.

189
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:40,837
He has to do a project, so
we came up with this idea.

190
00:21:40,920 --> 00:21:43,377
But if you ask me, he's
just doing it for Yui.

191
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:44,989
You're spoiling me, Daddy!

192
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:56,300
Nice job, guys!

193
00:21:56,540 --> 00:22:00,422
We got the Holy Sword Excalibur
and Mjolnir, the lightning hammer!

194
00:22:00,660 --> 00:22:02,380
Congrats to 2025!

195
00:22:03,080 --> 00:22:03,910
To us!

196
00:22:04,060 --> 00:22:04,960
To us!

197
00:22:07,100 --> 00:22:11,740
Hey, I was wondering, why did they
call it Excalibur in the game? Huh?

198
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:13,117
What do you mean, why?

199
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:14,030
Well,

200
00:22:14,113 --> 00:22:16,057
usually in the fantasy
books and comics I've read,

201
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:18,860
it's always called
Caliburn, not Excalibur.

202
00:22:19,040 --> 00:22:21,420
Oh, I don't know. No way!

203
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:25,169
You don't seem like someone
who'd be a fan of fantasy books.

204
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:28,897
When I was in middle school, I
pretty much lived at the library.

205
00:22:28,980 --> 00:22:32,157
I spent all my time there
reading books about King Arthur.

206
00:22:32,240 --> 00:22:34,887
Every one of them referred
to it as Caliburn.

207
00:22:35,060 --> 00:22:39,137
Actually, didn't the sword go by a lot of
different names in most of those legends?

208
00:22:39,220 --> 00:22:41,177
Depending on which Celtic language.

209
00:22:41,260 --> 00:22:43,057
But the word caliber is cool because it's

210
00:22:43,140 --> 00:22:45,237
what you call the
diameter of a gun barrel.

211
00:22:45,320 --> 00:22:48,897
And it's also how you describe the
quality of a person's character.

212
00:22:48,980 --> 00:22:50,337
Thanks for the lesson, Teach.

213
00:22:50,420 --> 00:22:52,420
Sorry if I got carried away there.

214
00:22:52,520 --> 00:22:54,377
So basically what you're saying is,

215
00:22:54,460 --> 00:22:59,740
whoever owns Excalibur has to be someone
who's an exceptional person. Huh? Who is?

216
00:22:59,940 --> 00:23:00,881
You mean Kirito?

217
00:23:01,140 --> 00:23:02,497
Yeah, of course. Duh.

218
00:23:02,580 --> 00:23:04,286
In fact, he's so exceptional,

219
00:23:04,460 --> 00:23:06,077
he wouldn't think twice about paying for

220
00:23:06,160 --> 00:23:08,477
dinner with some of that
crazy money he made,

221
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:09,390
right?

222
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:16,240
Yeah, I was saving it for a
surprise, but yeah, totally.

223
00:23:16,440 --> 00:23:17,616
This dinner's on me.

224
00:23:35,320 --> 00:23:37,700
Next time, The Forest House.
